course: dictionary
lesson: 5340
title: Ki: a word, a piece, a belief
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words stand on their own, and some are only pieces of longer words. «ki» is both. In Japanese and Korean, ki is a word for life energy or inner strength, the power people use in martial arts like aikido and karate. In Chinese the same idea is called «qi» or «chi».
explain: Look at the sentences about the made-up languages Kel and Selk. «In Kel, pa = 1, ki = 2, ro = 3, mu = 4 and lan = 5; a number before lan multiplies it, so ki lan = 10.» Here you can work out the meaning from the rules, and each word gets its meaning from the words around it.
explain: «In Selk, the describing word comes first: ki (eye) + ota (water) = kiota (tears, "eye-water").» Selk puts the describing word first, so ki is an eye. Once you know a word's parts, you can work out what a new word means.
explain: Ki as life energy is a belief from East Asian traditions. It is not something science has measured, so a teacher can talk about it, but it is not a fact in science.
fact: Ki is a word from Japanese and Korean, and it means life energy or inner strength.
fact: In Chinese, the same idea is called «qi» or «chi».
fact: «ki» is also a piece of longer English words, such as «kick», «kite» and «ski».
fact: «ki» is allowed in some Scrabble word lists, but it is not an everyday English word on its own.
fact: In Kel, «ki lan» means 10, because ki = 2 and a number before lan multiplies it.
exercise: «In Kel, ki = 2, and a number before lan multiplies it.» What is ki lan? | 7 | 25 | 11 | *10
exercise: «In Selk, ki (eye) + ota (water) = kiota.» What does kiota mean? | Water from the sea | *Tears, or eye-water | Rain | Eye of a fish
exercise: Which longer word contains the piece «ki»? | *kite | window | door | apple
test: What does the martial arts sense say about ki? | It is an English verb | It is measured with a ruler in science | *It is a belief from East Asian traditions, not something science has measured | It is a kind of fish
test: «In Selk, fen (fire) + mor (mountain) = fenmor.» What is fenmor? | Fire-water | *A fire-mountain, which is a volcano | A river | A tree
exam: «In Kel, ki lan pa» equals what? | *11 | 10 | 12 | 16
